<h2>dews-sourcegraph — A Skill That Hands Internal Code Search to Claude</h2>

<p>Any organization running SourceGraph in-house keeps meeting the same moment. Something of the same kind as the feature you are building almost certainly exists somewhere in the company, but that repository is not on your machine. So you open the web UI, run a search, skim the results with your eyes, and then explain them back to Claude — a round trip. <strong>dews-sourcegraph removes that round trip</strong> — Claude queries the internal instance itself, gets back <code>repo │ file:line │ snippet</code>, and carries the implementation forward citing that evidence as it stands.</p>

<p>The obstacle is authentication. A private instance blocks anonymous access with a 401, so an ordinary web-fetch tool reads nothing at all. This skill therefore performs a browser form login once, by itself, and caches the session it gets for reuse. There is no step where a person opens devtools and copies a cookie out.</p>

